{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-tuned weights for the transparent fire-source scorer.",
    "score_c = bias_c + sum_i(weight[i][c] * evidence_i), then softmax(score / temperature).",
    "Every evidence term is bounded to [0,1] so weights stay directly comparable.",
    "This file is the model. Changing it changes model_version (a hash of the",
    "file), so a tuning change is as traceable as a code change and needs no",
    "redeploy. Phase 8 swaps the whole thing for a trained model behind the",
    "identical output contract.",
    "",
    "Spec Rule 8: probabilities, never certainty. Spec Rule 3: nearby industry",
    "does not prove industrial origin, which is why no single term can win",
    "alone.",
    "Spec Rule 2: weather describes conditions, not source - so weather terms",
    "carry deliberately small class weights and are routed into severity",
    "instead. Giving temperature anomaly a large industrial weight would",
    "produce confidently wrong answers."
  ],
  "model_name": "rules-v1",
  "temperature": 1.7,
  "probability_floor": 0.02,
